  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 505.12 K, melting point of Sn; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.680$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.838 + 0.074 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.560 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.838\\times10^{-3}T+0.037\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.560\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.826$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-505.12 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 11.555 - 0.301 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 2.465 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 29.450 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 11.555 + 0.301 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 2.465 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 14.725 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 21.735 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n505.12-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ}=9.590-1.524\\times10^{-3}T-0.304\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+207.250T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 9.590 + 1.524 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.304 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 103.625 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 24.713 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Mills (80). ",
